# Charter

Norm for new code, humans and agents. Stack rules sit beside this file, loaded on matching files.

- Cite rules by `[ID]`, never by line. IDs never change nor get reused.
- Regimes: **checked** (`charter` fails: after edit, before commit, CI); **ratchet** (debt budget in `charter.toml` only goes down; lower it in the commit reducing the debt); **review** (`charter --unverified`).
- Conflict order: security and data integrity > published API contract > readability > form.
- **[WAIVERS]** Deliberate deviation: `ion repo waive <RULE> --reason "…"` (`kiln-waivers.toml`), never silent. Lasts a week, then 1, 3, 6 months per renewal; expired covers nothing. Generated file frozen: `ion repo waive <file>`. Never add or renew without the user's explicit agreement, nor to pass a check. Not waivable: [PERSONAL-DATA], [SECRETS], [NO-COMMIT-ON-MAIN], [LOCKED-DEPENDENCIES].
- **[REPORT-TO-ION-REPO]** Defect in what ion-repo provides (generated file, charter rule, plugin skill or hook, reusable workflow): not fixed here, `ion repo update` would undo it. `/repo:report`: PR if fix clear and local, else issue. Public under the user's account: only with explicit agreement, in English, nothing private.

## Size
- **[FILE-SIZE]** Max 300 lines per file (ratchet).
{%- if frontend in ['nuxt', 'next', 'astro', 'vite-react'] %} Growing {{ {'nuxt': 'Vue', 'next': 'React', 'astro': 'Astro', 'vite-react': 'React'}[frontend] }} component: directory (entry point + sub-components).
{%- endif %}
{%- if back_py or front_py %} Growing Python module: package whose `__init__.py` re-exports the public API.
{%- endif %}
{%- if java %} Growing Java class: split into single-responsibility classes.{% endif %} Exempt: generated files, those `.gitattributes` marks `linguist-generated` (only list).
- **[FUNCTION-SIZE]** One responsibility, max 30 lines (excluding component templates, docstrings); test max 40 if splitting hides the scenario.
{%- if level >= 1 %}
- **[ONE-CLASS]** One class per file. Exceptions, still under [FILE-SIZE]: one domain's schemas, one domain's exceptions, one test file's test classes.
{%- endif %}

## Names
- **[GENERIC-NAMES]** Never `data`, `df`, `res`, `val`, `tmp`, `info`, `obj`, `item`, `result` alone, `x`; say what it holds (`sales_by_month`). Except parameters imposed by a framework signature.
- **[VOCABULARY]** Code in English, domain words; user-read text in project language. URLs are public, may differ from code.
- **[BOOLEANS]** Prefix:
{%- if front_js %} `is`, `has`, `should`, `can` in TypeScript (`isLoading`);{% endif %}
{%- if java %} `is`, `has`, `should`, `can` in Java (`isFull`);{% endif %}
{%- if back_py or front_py or not (java or front_js) %} `is_`, `has_`, `should_`, `can_` in Python (`is_active`){% endif %}.
{%- if api %} Published API fields stay ([FROZEN-CONTRACT]).{% endif %}
- **[CASE]** Classes PascalCase; constants `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`;
{%- if back_py or front_py %} Python functions/variables snake_case;{% endif %}
{%- if java %} Java methods/variables camelCase, packages lowercase;{% endif %}
{%- if front_js %} components PascalCase prefixed by domain (`ChartLegend`, `MapTooltip`);{% endif %} files per language convention.

## Values
- **[NO-MAGIC-VALUES]** No business literal (status, role, threshold, delay, price, colour, repeated column name):
{%- if front_js %} front: `{{ {'nuxt': 'app/utils/constants.ts', 'next': 'lib/constants.ts', 'astro': 'src/constants.ts', 'vite-react': 'src/constants.ts'}[frontend] }}` or TS enums;{% endif %}
{%- if backend == 'django' %} backend: `TextChoices`/`IntegerChoices` or named module constant.
{%- elif java %} Java: `enum` or named `static final`{% if front_py %}; Python: `enum.StrEnum` or named constant{% endif %}.
{%- else %} Python: `enum.StrEnum` or named module constant.{% endif %} Allowed: `0`, `1`, `-1`, `""`, `None`, indexes, test literals.
- **[MONEY]** Integer minor units (`*_cents`) in database, API, front; never float; convert only for display.
- **[TIME-ZONE]** Store instants in UTC. Calendar notions (today, day, month, period bounds) in `{{ timezone }}`
{%- if backend == 'django' %} (`timezone.localdate()`){% elif java %} (`ZoneId.of("{{ timezone }}")`){% elif back_py or front_py %} (`ZoneInfo("{{ timezone }}")`){% endif %}, never `.date()` on a UTC instant.

## Personal data, secrets
- **[PERSONAL-DATA]** No personal data (email, name, phone, ID document, full IP) in logs, errors, URLs, cache keys, figures: log `user_id`.
{%- if level >= 2 %} New stored personal data: same change covers export and anonymisation required by law (GDPR in Europe).
{%- endif %}
- **[SECRETS]** No secret in code or repo; use environment
